# Bug, as the owner settled it on 9 Nov 2026: Find the cause, Fix, Test and deliver.
# Each step is a plan group, and `gate` names the fact Fleet sees for itself that ends it: his approval
# of the plan, of a walk, of a sketch or of a page, Checks green at the pushed commit, the merge, or none.
# Fleet sends the groups to the agent on its first turn and keeps only the gates; nothing moves a Job
# backwards. `.claude/decisions/2026-11-09-workflows-are-gated-plan-groups.md` has each answer and the
# dry run behind it.
#
# Where the reasoning lives: `crates/core-model/domain/workflowdef-fields.toml` is the schema,
# `docs/concepts/workflow.md` the concept, `docs/concepts/session/the-plan.md` the gates,
# `crates/config/src/workflow.rs` the parser. These files are YAML and the `.json` extension is kept on
# purpose: a `#` comment is not JSON. `workflow-samples/bug.json` is the designed seven-step form, not a
# duplicate of this one; do not reconcile the two. This file is also what Armada ships.
#
# **No test order is imposed.** "Write no tests yet" contradicted briefs that ask for a failing test
# first; the plan says the order.
#
# **Tests fold into delivery, which ends at the merge whatever the delivery** (9 Nov 2026): at work a
# draft pull request goes to a test environment, and what he finds there comes back to the same Job.
#
# **`deliver` is gated `human_always`** for the old rail, which a later change removes; Fleet does not
# enforce it. Every definition here declares `for_requests`, read off its own criteria; `fleet`'s
# `tests::proposing` refuses one without.
{
  "version": 1,
  "workflow_id": "bug",
  "name": "bug",
  "for_requests": "Something that is broken: it used to work, or is meant to work, and does not, and what is wanted is the cause found and fixed. Taking a change that already landed back out whole is a revert, and adding or changing what the software does on purpose is a feature.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "find_the_cause",
      "label": "Find the cause",
      "about": "Reproduces the bug, names the cause and writes down the fix as a plan. Ends when you approve the plan.",
      "instructions": "Reproduce the bug. Find why it happens, not only where it shows, and name the root cause with file:line.\nPropose the fix beside it, with its tasks in the order they must happen. Say `seen: true` in record_plan when the person would see any piece of the change.\nName the files you expect to touch, and end with what you could not settle, each with file:line evidence.\nRecord the plan with record_plan and wait for the person to approve it. Edit nothing before then but a mock.",
      "gate": "plan_approved",
      "asks_delivery": true,
      "delivers": false,
      "advance_gate": "auto"
    },
    {
      "id": "fix",
      "label": "Fix",
      "about": "Makes the fix and shows it to you as a short walk straight to the place. Ends when you approve the walk. Left out when nothing would be seen.",
      "instructions": "Make the smallest change that addresses the cause, following the plan. A small correction is yours to make and to say; a change of approach goes to the person.\nShow the fix as a short walk straight to the place with show_window, naming this group, and wait for the person's approval. Leave this group out of the plan when the project serves no walk or nothing would be seen.\nShow a walk once. Do not show one he approved again.",
      "gate": "walk_approved",
      "delivers": false,
      "advance_gate": "auto"
    },
    {
      "id": "deliver",
      "label": "Test and deliver",
      "about": "Proves the fix with a test that fails without it, and delivers it the way you chose. Ends at the merge.",
      "instructions": "Where the Fix group was left out, make the fix here first.\nWrite a test that fails without the fix, for the reported reason, and passes with it.\nPush the branch and open a draft pull request while the checks run locally. Fix what is red. A test that is also red on main is not this Job's to fix: look up who is fixing main, say so, and carry on.\nDeliver by the delivery the person chose, and do not ask again. Auto land: mark the pull request ready and merge it on a green ci. Open PR: leave it open; the Job stays until it merges, so what the person finds in a test environment comes back here. Keep local: push nothing, and record this group's gate as none.\nReport the branch, what is on it, and what the person needs before merging.",
      "gate": "merged",
      "delivers": true,
      "advance_gate": "human_always"
    }
  ]
}
